  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37143978",
      "title": "Adding Cross-Screen Navigation",
      "lectureOrder": 162,
      "videoOrder": 150,
      "sourceHash": "b929ce11b1989c1b932ed068835db333e91d0db5ae2ebac217e19354eaf2d181",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 4.38,
          "en": "So at this point we can output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.38,
          "end": 8.58,
          "en": "this basic unstyled and unfinished meals list here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.58,
          "end": 11.34,
          "en": "this meals screen to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.34,
          "end": 14.37,
          "en": "But of course at the moment this is all hardcoded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.37,
          "end": 18.06,
          "en": "In main Dart, I always output the meals screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.06,
          "end": 21.54,
          "en": "with all my dummy meals and a hardcoded title.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.54,
          "end": 22.803,
          "en": "That's not the goal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.67,
          "end": 28.67,
          "en": "Instead, the goal is to, here, output the CategoriesScreen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.13,
          "end": 30.72,
          "en": "as we did it before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.72,
          "end": 33.39,
          "en": "and to then make sure that if we tap a category,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.39,
          "end": 37.35,
          "en": "we're navigated to that category's meals screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.35,
          "end": 40.38,
          "en": "which then only shows the meals for that category.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.38,
          "end": 43.13,
          "en": "And that's therefore what we're going to implement now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.46,
          "end": 46.857,
          "en": "For that, as a first step, we can get rid of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.857,
          "end": 50.52,
          "en": "the meals screen import here in the main Dart file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.52,
          "end": 53.04,
          "en": "and of the dummy data import there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.04,
          "end": 55.71,
          "en": "And instead go to the categories.dart file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.71,
          "end": 58.113,
          "en": "where we have this categories screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.04,
          "end": 61.89,
          "en": "And there, I want to add a new method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.89,
          "end": 65.013,
          "en": "and I'll name this method _selectCategory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.18,
          "end": 70.2,
          "en": "And it won't return any data, hence its return type is void.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.2,
          "end": 72.27,
          "en": "And here, we're doing something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.27,
          "end": 74.55,
          "en": "we haven't really done before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.55,
          "end": 78.003,
          "en": "We are adding a method to a StatelessWidget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.003,
          "end": 80.58,
          "en": "Now, we haven't done this before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.58,
          "end": 84.42,
          "en": "because in most cases when we added a method to a widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.42,
          "end": 88.5,
          "en": "so when we reacted to a button tap, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.5,
          "end": 90.84,
          "en": "we wanted to update some state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.84,
          "end": 94.14,
          "en": "And of course we can't do that in a StatelessWidget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.14,
          "end": 97.02000000000001,
          "en": "But here, we don't want to update state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.02000000000001,
          "end": 99.87,
          "en": "Instead, I want to load a different screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.87,
          "end": 103.32,
          "en": "And for this, we can use a feature built into Flutter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.32,
          "end": 106.35,
          "en": "We can use the Navigator class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.35,
          "end": 109.443,
          "en": "which you already saw earlier in the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.34,
          "end": 113.49000000000001,
          "en": "Earlier in the course, we used it with its pop method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.49000000000001,
          "end": 117.27000000000001,
          "en": "to remove a screen and go back to another screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 117.27000000000001,
          "end": 118.5,
          "en": "even though you didn't know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.5,
          "end": 122.67,
          "en": "that we were kind of working with screens back then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.67,
          "end": 125.58,
          "en": "But this modal, which we for example closed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.58,
          "end": 129.09,
          "en": "in the end also was kind of like a screen that was opened.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 129.09,
          "end": 132.243,
          "en": "And with Navigator.pop, we were able to close it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.29,
          "end": 135.57,
          "en": "Now we don't want to close a screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 135.57,
          "end": 138.66,
          "en": "but instead we want to navigate to a screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 138.66,
          "end": 143.01,
          "en": "And this can be done by using the push method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 143.01,
          "end": 146.64,
          "en": "Now the push method wants a context value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 146.64,
          "end": 149.85,
          "en": "and then a route value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 149.85,
          "end": 152.22,
          "en": "And in the end, what push will do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 152.22,
          "end": 154.62,
          "en": "is it will push this route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 154.62,
          "end": 158.22,
          "en": "which in the end kind of will be a widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 158.22,
          "end": 162.09,
          "en": "on top of the current stack of screens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 162.09,
          "end": 164.28,
          "en": "And this can be a bit of a strange term",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 164.28,
          "end": 166.53,
          "en": "when you hear it for the first time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 166.53,
          "end": 168.06,
          "en": "But in the end, in Flutter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 168.06,
          "end": 171.75,
          "en": "navigation basically works with screen stacks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 171.75,
          "end": 175.65,
          "en": "You can think of the screens being organized as layers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 175.65,
          "end": 177.3,
          "en": "put on top of each other.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 177.3,
          "end": 181.35,
          "en": "And as a user, you always see the topmost layer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 181.35,
          "end": 183.57,
          "en": "the topmost screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 183.57,
          "end": 185.19,
          "en": "So, that's why it's called push.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 185.19,
          "end": 189.18,
          "en": "You push a new layer onto this stack of screens,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 189.18,
          "end": 190.33,
          "en": "which you already have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 191.55,
          "end": 194.79,
          "en": "And on the other hand, if you pop a screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 194.79,
          "end": 196.71,
          "en": "you remove one of these layers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 196.71,
          "end": 200.43,
          "en": "And since the user always sees the topmost layer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 200.43,
          "end": 202.47,
          "en": "the user then sees the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 202.47,
          "end": 204.63,
          "en": "below the screen that was popped off.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 204.63,
          "end": 206.85,
          "en": "That's the idea here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 206.85,
          "end": 209.28,
          "en": "So here we're pushing, and we need to pass in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 209.28,
          "end": 211.683,
          "en": "a context and a route, as you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 212.88,
          "end": 215.16,
          "en": "Now, since I'm in a StatelessWidget here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 215.16,
          "end": 218.43,
          "en": "context is not globally available.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 218.43,
          "end": 221.28,
          "en": "You might recall that in the state objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 221.28,
          "end": 223.71,
          "en": "that belonged to Stateful widgets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 223.71,
          "end": 227.1,
          "en": "a context property was globally available,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 227.1,
          "end": 229.53,
          "en": "and could therefore be used in all the methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 229.53,
          "end": 231.453,
          "en": "Here, that's not the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 232.29,
          "end": 236.79,
          "en": "Therefore here, we indeed must accept context value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 236.79,
          "end": 239.1,
          "en": "which must be of type BuildContext",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 239.1,
          "end": 242.34,
          "en": "in this select category function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 242.34,
          "end": 245.703,
          "en": "so that we can pass context as a value to push.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 246.78,
          "end": 248.52,
          "en": "By the way, alternatively,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 248.52,
          "end": 252.63,
          "en": "you can also call Navigator.of(context).push,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 252.63,
          "end": 255.03,
          "en": "and then only pass the route to push.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 255.03,
          "end": 259.14,
          "en": "This is in the end, the same as writing this code like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 259.14,
          "end": 262.02,
          "en": "and it is up to you which approach you prefer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 262.02,
          "end": 264.06,
          "en": "I'm just putting this out there because you'll see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 264.06,
          "end": 267.273,
          "en": "this kind of code in a lot of Flutter projects as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 268.41,
          "end": 270.48,
          "en": "But that's how you then push a new screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 270.48,
          "end": 273.06,
          "en": "onto this stack of screens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 273.06,
          "end": 275.013,
          "en": "But what's up with this route now?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 276.18,
          "end": 278.22,
          "en": "Well, such a route is created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 278.22,
          "end": 282.72,
          "en": "by instantiating a MaterialPageRoute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 282.72,
          "end": 286.23,
          "en": "Som by creating a MaterialPageRoute object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 286.23,
          "end": 288.9,
          "en": "with help of the MaterialPageRoute class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 288.9,
          "end": 291.24,
          "en": "which is provided by Flutter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 291.24,
          "end": 292.95,
          "en": "And this gives us such a route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 292.95,
          "end": 295.40999999999997,
          "en": "that can be pushed onto this stack.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 295.40999999999997,
          "end": 298.62,
          "en": "And as you can see, since I used autocompletion here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 298.62,
          "end": 300.96,
          "en": "this wants a builder parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 300.96,
          "end": 304.14,
          "en": "which wants a function that gives us a context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 304.14,
          "end": 306.57,
          "en": "So, we will get a context automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 306.57,
          "end": 308.16,
          "en": "in this builder function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 308.16,
          "end": 311.55,
          "en": "and we should return a widget as part of this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 311.55,
          "end": 314.22,
          "en": "And that widget will be that screen widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 314.22,
          "end": 315.47,
          "en": "that should be displayed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 316.53,
          "end": 318.3,
          "en": "So here, I have a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 318.3,
          "end": 321.81,
          "en": "that automatically receives some context object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 321.81,
          "end": 326.733,
          "en": "and in there I then return my MealsScreen, in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 328.14,
          "end": 332.733,
          "en": "Now for this to work, we also must import this MealsScreen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 334.02,
          "end": 337.26,
          "en": "So here, from the screens folder, I'll import meals.dart,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 337.26,
          "end": 340.08299999999997,
          "en": "so that MealsScreen is available here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 340.92,
          "end": 343.59000000000003,
          "en": "And now of course, we still must provide a title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 343.59000000000003,
          "end": 344.94,
          "en": "and then our meals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 344.94,
          "end": 346.83,
          "en": "That hasn't changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 346.83,
          "end": 349.53,
          "en": "So, for the moment I'll just say Some title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 349.53,
          "end": 351.51,
          "en": "and pass an empty list of meals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 351.51,
          "end": 353.85,
          "en": "Though this will change later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 353.85,
          "end": 355.44,
          "en": "But for the moment, that's it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 355.44,
          "end": 358.35,
          "en": "And this is how we would push this meals screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 358.35,
          "end": 360.63,
          "en": "on top of this stack of pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 360.63,
          "end": 363.57,
          "en": "And since it would therefore be the topmost screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 363.57,
          "end": 365.883,
          "en": "it would be the screen users see.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 367.32,
          "end": 368.465,
          "en": "But of course, right now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 368.465,
          "end": 371.25,
          "en": "selectCategory never gets executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 371.25,
          "end": 374.25,
          "en": "So, we have to make sure that it does get executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 374.25,
          "end": 378.15,
          "en": "by connecting it to our CategoryGridItem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 378.15,
          "end": 381.12,
          "en": "Or to be precise, by connecting it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 381.12,
          "end": 384.36,
          "en": "to this onTap parameter here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 384.36,
          "end": 387.003,
          "en": "inside of our CategoryGridItem widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 388.71,
          "end": 390.78,
          "en": "Well, and you learned how that works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 390.78,
          "end": 392.76,
          "en": "inside of CategoryGridItem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 392.76,
          "end": 395.673,
          "en": "you can simply expect to get a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 396.87,
          "end": 399.33299999999997,
          "en": "which could be called onSelectCategory.",
          "zh": ""
